  { name:"Withlacoochee State Forest Visitor Center (permits & info)", category:"workspace", county:"Hernando", st:"FL", lat:28.63778, lng:-82.33962, city:"Brooksville", url:"https://www.fdacs.gov/Forest-Wildfire/Our-Forests/State-Forests/Withlacoochee-State-Forest", address:"15003 Broad St, Brooksville, FL 34601-4201", phone:"(352) 797-4140", org:"Florida Dept. of Agriculture & Consumer Services — Florida Forest Service", verified:"2026-08-03", services:["workspace"], notes:"Start here before camping anywhere on the Croom Tract below — this office issues the State Forest Use Authorization required for any organized/group activity, including a group of 6+ people camping. Solo/small-group primitive camping in the designated zones doesn't need a permit, but calling first confirms current conditions (burn bans, closures). Mon–Fri 8am–noon & 1–4:30pm, closed holidays." },
  { name:"Silver Lake Campground (Withlacoochee State Forest, Croom Tract)", category:"camping", county:"Hernando", st:"FL", lat:28.57361, lng:-82.22222, city:"Brooksville", url:"https://floridastateforests.reserveamerica.com/camping/silver-lake-campground-withlacoochee-state-forest/", address:"31475 Silver Lake Road, Brooksville, FL 34602", phone:"(352) 797-4140", org:"Florida Forest Service", verified:"2026-08-03", when:"Day-use gate: 8am–8pm. Registered campers get an after-hours gate code on their reservation confirmation, so a paid overnight stay isn't cut off by the day-use closing time — this is the one camping entry on this map where that's actually confirmed, not just assumed.", services:["showers"], notes:"Developed campground, 23 sites, $13.45/night (RV or tent) — full water/electric (30 & 50 amp) hookups at every site, a bathhouse with real showers, dump station, boat ramp, and Withlacoochee State Trail access. 3 sites (19–21) have enhanced accessibility. Reserve via ReserveAmerica (1-877-879-3859) or call the Visitor Center — cheapest legal, amenity-having overnight option in the county's public land system, and the shower access alone makes it worth knowing about even without an overnight stay in mind. DIRECTIONS: same general area as the Croom Tract primitive zones — via I-75 Exit 301, east on SR-50/US-98, north on Croom-Rital Rd; via Suncoast Parkway (589), north to SR-50, east through Brooksville, north on US-41 to Croom Rd (CR-480), then follow signage to Silver Lake Road." },
  { name:"Croom Tract Primitive Camp Zone East (free, hike-in)", category:"camping", county:"Hernando", st:"FL", lat:28.59667, lng:-82.23861, city:"Brooksville", url:"https://floridastateforests.reserveamerica.com/camping/croom-tract-primitive-camp-zone-east/", address:"Trailhead: Tucker Hill Trailhead, 26578 Croom Rd, Brooksville, FL 34601 — camp zone is a ~0.5 mile hike in from the parking area, marked by yellow bands on trees", phone:"(352) 797-4140", org:"Florida Forest Service", verified:"2026-08-03", when:"Day-use/trailhead parking: sunrise–sunset (statewide Florida Forest Service policy) — overnight camping itself is the sanctioned exception to that, but it wasn't possible to independently confirm whether the Tucker Hill parking area's vehicle gate physically locks at sunset. Call the Visitor Center (352-797-4140) before an overnight hike-in to make sure your car won't be locked in/out.", services:[], notes:"No camping fee for a solo camper or small group (Authorization only required for groups of 6+ — see Visitor Center entry); a separate $2/person day-use entrance fee (or $45 annual day-use pass) may apply just to park at the Tucker Hill trailhead regardless of camping — unconfirmed whether that's waived for registered overnight campers, ask when you call. Hike-in/hike-out only — no vehicle access to the camp zone itself. No water, no restrooms, no amenities beyond occasional fire rings/picnic tables at existing sites. Only cooking fires permitted. This is the more accessible of the two primitive zones (0.5 mi vs. 5.25 mi hike). DIRECTIONS to Tucker Hill Trailhead — via I-75: Exit 301, head east on SR-50/US-98, turn north on Croom-Rital Rd, continue ~8.5 miles. Via Suncoast Parkway (589): take it north to SR-50, head east through Brooksville, then north on US-41 (Broad St) to Croom Rd (CR-480), turn right/east ~5 miles to the trailhead." },
  { name:"Croom Tract Primitive Camp Zone West (free, hike-in)", category:"camping", county:"Hernando", st:"FL", lat:28.59833, lng:-82.29611, city:"Brooksville", url:"https://floridastateforests.reserveamerica.com/camping/croom-tract-primitive-camp-zone-west/", address:"Trailhead: Tucker Hill Trailhead, 26578 Croom Rd, Brooksville, FL 34601 — camp zone is a ~5.25 mile hike in from the parking area", phone:"(352) 797-4140", org:"Florida Forest Service", verified:"2026-08-03", when:"Day-use/trailhead parking: sunrise–sunset (statewide Florida Forest Service policy) — same unconfirmed gate-locking caveat as the East zone entry; call ahead.", services:[], notes:"Same free-camping/permit rules and possible $2/person day-use parking fee as the East zone, but a much longer hike in (5.25 miles) — realistically only workable with backpacking gear. No water, no amenities. Only cooking fires permitted. Same DIRECTIONS to Tucker Hill Trailhead as the East zone entry (shared trailhead) — via I-75: Exit 301, head east on SR-50/US-98, turn north on Croom-Rital Rd, continue ~8.5 miles. Via Suncoast Parkway (589): take it north to SR-50, head east through Brooksville, then north on US-41 (Broad St) to Croom Rd (CR-480), turn right/east ~5 miles to the trailhead." },
  { name:"Chassahowitzka River Campground (out of county, nearby)", category:"camping", county:"Citrus", st:"FL", lat:28.72333, lng:-82.60333, city:"Chassahowitzka", url:"https://chassahowitzkaflorida.com", address:"8600 W Miss Maggie Dr, Chassahowitzka, FL 34448", phone:"(352) 382-2200", org:"Citrus County Parks & Recreation", notes:"Just across the Citrus County line, included because it's the nearest fee campground to the parts of Hernando County where the WMA itself (Chassahowitzka Wildlife Management Area, overnight camping NOT permitted there) is the closest public land. 53 full-hookup RV sites plus 28 primitive tent sites, boat ramp, general store. Call for current nightly rates — not listed publicly." }
